WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:35.400


00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:39.060
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:00:40.145 --> 00:00:43.481
AS GROUP
COMPANY FALL RETREAT

00:00:57.287 --> 00:00:59.205
You know, when I'm in a good mood,

00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:01.082
I eat vegetables.

00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:09.174
Have you eaten yet, Ye-ji?

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:11.176
Eat lots of vegetables.

00:01:18.892 --> 00:01:20.602
There are no vegetables.

00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:28.443
THE LOYAL CATERING

00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:33.823
Salute!

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.454
-Hello, can I get your name?
-Byeon Eun-a.

00:02:37.762 --> 00:02:38.972
Eun-a!

00:02:39.055 --> 00:02:40.640
Eun-a, over here.

00:02:56.614 --> 00:02:58.950
XIMFIT WILL ANALYZE EMOTIONS
YOU DIDN'T EVEN KNOW YOU HAD

00:04:06.559 --> 00:04:09.604
I was categorized
as an unemployed male in his forties.

00:04:09.687 --> 00:04:10.897
What about you, Eun-a?

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.024
A female in her thirties
with psychological issues.

00:04:15.109 --> 00:04:16.069
I'm serious.

00:04:16.152 --> 00:04:19.739
Did Lee Jun-hwan
specifically describe you that way?

00:04:19.822 --> 00:04:21.616
No, someone else introduced me to this.

00:04:22.658 --> 00:04:25.078
Nobody at work knows
I'm wearing this watch.

00:04:25.161 --> 00:04:26.537
Oh, right, I see.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.958
They said this could help people
with psychological issues.

00:04:35.713 --> 00:04:37.590
Psychological issues?

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.347
You've got a word
that makes your heart pound, don't you?

00:04:46.349 --> 00:04:47.683
I had no idea

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.019
the word "unemployed"
would make my heart pound so much.

00:04:50.645 --> 00:04:54.899
When my heart rate goes up,
and warning beeps go off,

00:04:54.982 --> 00:04:56.401
my heart pounds even more.

00:04:56.484 --> 00:04:58.236
Knowing that it's pounding
makes it pound more.

00:04:59.612 --> 00:05:00.738
It feels like,

00:05:01.739 --> 00:05:02.782
"Oh, I've been caught."

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.660
You haven't experienced it yet, have you?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.872
You'll discover a word
that makes your heart pound.

00:05:11.207 --> 00:05:13.000
Just hearing that makes my heart race.

00:05:14.293 --> 00:05:16.379
So you do have a word
that makes your heart pound?

00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:18.714
I have too many.

00:05:19.966 --> 00:05:21.300
They're not words

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:24.053
-so much as they are names.
-Names?

00:05:24.637 --> 00:05:25.471
The names

00:05:26.514 --> 00:05:27.723
of the men who left me.

00:05:29.225 --> 00:05:30.268
"Men"?

00:05:30.935 --> 00:05:31.894
Plural?

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:35.606
Whenever I hear the name of anyone
who wrote me off,

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.860
my heart pounds immediately.

00:05:38.943 --> 00:05:41.154
Gosh, the mere thought makes it pound.

00:05:42.905 --> 00:05:43.781
I don't react

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:46.284
to names at all.

00:05:46.951 --> 00:05:48.202
Your relationships must be nice and neat.

00:05:48.828 --> 00:05:50.913
They're actually nice and messed up

00:05:52.123 --> 00:05:54.208
because everyone has written me off.

00:05:56.961 --> 00:05:58.713
All names disrespect me,

00:05:58.796 --> 00:06:00.339
and I disrespect all names.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.968
Thanks to this watch,

00:06:04.051 --> 00:06:08.890
I've realized that I don't like anyone
or anything in this world.

00:06:08.973 --> 00:06:10.558
Except for food.

00:06:10.641 --> 00:06:12.935
Food is the only thing I respect and love.

00:06:14.353 --> 00:06:17.815
My favorite writing is what's on a menu.

00:06:18.441 --> 00:06:20.568
There's nothing more beautiful than that.

00:06:23.988 --> 00:06:25.072
Wearing this watch

00:06:25.948 --> 00:06:27.283
made one thing very clear.

00:06:27.867 --> 00:06:30.578
I'm a destructive person.

00:06:36.918 --> 00:06:37.835
You see…

00:06:39.545 --> 00:06:42.298
there was a moment
that made me really trust this watch.

00:06:42.381 --> 00:06:44.717
I went to a café the other day,

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.678
and all of a sudden,
I heard a screech and a thud.

00:06:49.513 --> 00:06:51.807
I'd never heard anything like that
so up close before.

00:06:51.891 --> 00:06:53.601
-Oh no.
-I didn't see you.

00:06:53.684 --> 00:06:54.852
I'll have my insurance take care of it.

00:06:54.936 --> 00:06:57.271
My heart was pounding like crazy
from the shock,

00:06:57.355 --> 00:07:00.066
so when this vibrated,
I didn't even think twice.

00:07:00.149 --> 00:07:03.486
I figured it'd be "fear" or "shock."

00:07:03.569 --> 00:07:05.613
But do you know what it said?

00:07:12.703 --> 00:07:14.372
EXCITED

00:07:14.455 --> 00:07:15.414
"Excited."

00:07:16.082 --> 00:07:17.583
No way.

00:07:17.667 --> 00:07:19.752
I had to cover it up before anyone saw it.

00:07:24.632 --> 00:07:27.301
I just accepted it at that point.

00:07:27.885 --> 00:07:30.179
That's right. I was excited.

00:07:32.056 --> 00:07:33.349
Jeez, Hwang Dong-man.

00:07:36.269 --> 00:07:39.105
There was a world leaders' summit
not too long ago.

00:07:39.188 --> 00:07:42.108
I woke up with a cold that morning,

00:07:42.191 --> 00:07:45.278
but I still worked a catering gig
for a 500-person luncheon

00:07:45.361 --> 00:07:47.029
and then taught a class in the evening.

00:07:47.113 --> 00:07:49.156
I barely made it home and just collapsed,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.616
but I had to look at my phone.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.617
Yeah.

00:07:52.118 --> 00:07:53.035
I think

00:07:53.536 --> 00:07:56.163
I'll check my phone even on my deathbed.

00:07:56.247 --> 00:07:59.333
Anyway, I was on my phone,
and I see there's been a terrorist attack.

00:07:59.917 --> 00:08:02.128
So I jumped up and turned on the TV.

00:08:02.211 --> 00:08:05.965
I saw special forces rushing in
and heard gunfire.

00:08:06.048 --> 00:08:09.343
And I thought to myself,
"If all those world leaders were to die,

00:08:09.427 --> 00:08:11.596
the world would finally fall apart."

00:08:13.264 --> 00:08:16.183
I'm watching in shock,
and you know what popped up on my watch?

00:08:16.851 --> 00:08:17.810
I think I know.

00:08:17.893 --> 00:08:19.145
"Thrilled."

00:08:20.313 --> 00:08:21.397
Oh jeez.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.357
I wasn't watching out of concern.

00:08:23.983 --> 00:08:25.818
I was about to die from exhaustion,

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:27.737
but suddenly, I was wide awake
and not tired at all.

00:08:29.113 --> 00:08:32.116
I forgot I was tired and kept watching.

00:08:33.618 --> 00:08:35.995
They rescued everyone,
and the terrorists were captured alive.

00:08:36.078 --> 00:08:38.497
-You know what popped up?
-Beep.

00:08:38.581 --> 00:08:41.125
No, I can't. I don't want to get it right.

00:08:41.709 --> 00:08:42.960
"Disappointed"?

00:08:47.465 --> 00:08:49.508
How could there be no casualties?

00:08:49.592 --> 00:08:52.345
I was exhausted,
but I watched it till the end.

00:08:52.428 --> 00:08:54.263
I deserved to see a dramatic ending.

00:08:54.889 --> 00:08:56.599
That's just the guy I am, and I accept it.

00:08:56.682 --> 00:08:58.267
This is who I am.

00:08:58.351 --> 00:08:59.560
Guilty as charged.

00:08:59.644 --> 00:09:02.146
Words like "love" or "peace"

00:09:02.897 --> 00:09:04.899
bore me to death.

00:09:05.816 --> 00:09:08.277
But "revenge," "destruction,"
or "retribution"?

00:09:08.361 --> 00:09:10.905
When I hear such words, my eyes sparkle.

00:09:11.489 --> 00:09:13.658
The best part about wearing this
was when I realized,

00:09:13.741 --> 00:09:15.201
"Hey, Hwang Dong-man."

00:09:15.868 --> 00:09:17.328
"You're a destructive person."

00:09:17.411 --> 00:09:19.914
It laid it out for me, nice and simple.

00:09:20.539 --> 00:09:24.001
So I decided to stop pretending
to be a good person.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.385
When Park Gyeong-se's movie tanked…

00:09:34.929 --> 00:09:36.389
I was truly happy.

00:09:36.972 --> 00:09:38.224
SISTER VENGEANCE

00:09:38.307 --> 00:09:39.850
Bad reviews were pouring in.

00:09:40.559 --> 00:09:41.936
And it was

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.521
really brutal.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.732
There was a certain satisfaction
in knowing

00:09:46.816 --> 00:09:49.443
the whole country realized
just how lame he really was.

00:09:51.237 --> 00:09:53.823
I cooked myself some fresh rice for once,

00:09:53.906 --> 00:09:56.867
and danced for the first time in my life.

00:09:56.951 --> 00:10:01.163
I felt guilt-free satisfaction
in someone else's misfortune.

00:10:03.833 --> 00:10:05.543
I realized, "So this is peace."

00:10:05.626 --> 00:10:07.336
Now, you might ask,

00:10:08.295 --> 00:10:09.463
"Aren't you two close?"

00:10:09.547 --> 00:10:10.381
Nope.

00:10:10.464 --> 00:10:12.550
We need to clarify the meaning of "close."

00:10:12.633 --> 00:10:15.010
We've just known each other
for a long time.

00:10:15.094 --> 00:10:18.180
We're well acquainted,
but we don't like each other.

00:10:18.889 --> 00:10:20.015
We used to be close.

00:10:21.809 --> 00:10:23.436
Back when we were all the same.

00:10:24.061 --> 00:10:25.771
When we were all nobodies

00:10:26.897 --> 00:10:29.358
sitting around together,
roasting other people's movies.

00:10:29.442 --> 00:10:32.611
Park Gyeong-se was the one
who talked the most trash back then.

00:10:33.404 --> 00:10:35.614
This is why it's getting bad reviews!

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.243
There's no storyline, and it's just noisy!

00:10:39.326 --> 00:10:40.494
What's this even about?

00:10:40.578 --> 00:10:41.704
Someone explain it to me.

00:10:43.664 --> 00:10:45.374
One by one, they made their debut.

00:10:45.458 --> 00:10:47.334
Look, over here. The transitions.

00:10:47.418 --> 00:10:49.003
-Jeez, did you see that?
-Damn it.

00:10:49.545 --> 00:10:51.255
You're going to break the TV!

00:10:53.591 --> 00:10:56.051
Now, the seven of them
get together to talk trash without me.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.221
Whenever I show up…

00:10:59.305 --> 00:11:00.181
Hey, you're here.

00:11:00.931 --> 00:11:02.266
They're indifferent.

00:11:03.934 --> 00:11:07.855
Like I'm not on their level anymore,
and they don't see me as worth debating.

00:11:10.316 --> 00:11:11.484
What a bunch of jerks.

00:11:16.113 --> 00:11:17.740
I'm starting to get upset.

00:11:21.869 --> 00:11:22.953
In any case,

00:11:23.037 --> 00:11:24.038
I, Hwang Dong-man,

00:11:25.581 --> 00:11:26.874
am a destructive person.

00:11:36.383 --> 00:11:37.551
You seem like someone

00:11:39.178 --> 00:11:41.722
with a thousand doors wide open.

00:11:48.479 --> 00:11:51.315
Imagine everyone
had a thousand doors inside them.

00:11:52.483 --> 00:11:56.445
Reading something written by someone
who hasn't even opened a single door

00:11:56.529 --> 00:11:57.696
is so boring and suffocating.

00:11:59.073 --> 00:12:03.786
But reading a screenplay by someone
with a few doors open grabs my attention.

00:12:04.537 --> 00:12:05.579
You seem like someone

00:12:07.289 --> 00:12:10.125
who's got all a thousand doors wide open.

00:12:17.341 --> 00:12:19.093
Then why'd you say those things

00:12:20.135 --> 00:12:21.136
last time?

00:12:22.179 --> 00:12:23.639
In front of Mr. Choi.

00:12:24.557 --> 00:12:28.060
The protagonist in Weather Maker
didn't feel like you.

00:12:30.187 --> 00:12:33.190
Well, that's because the protagonist
has to be cooler than me.

00:12:34.817 --> 00:12:36.610
You're way cooler.

00:12:44.118 --> 00:12:45.411
You're much more raw…

00:12:47.413 --> 00:12:48.455
and much warmer.

00:13:40.799 --> 00:13:42.676
I thought I'd feel better

00:13:43.218 --> 00:13:44.595
if I wore this watch.

00:13:45.429 --> 00:13:48.140
Like, "Oh, I'm feeling down right now.
Let's change that."

00:13:48.641 --> 00:13:50.267
I thought I could change my mood.

00:13:50.976 --> 00:13:52.311
But turns out, I can't.

00:13:52.394 --> 00:13:53.270
Nope.

00:13:53.354 --> 00:13:55.731
You can never force
your emotions to change.

00:13:56.357 --> 00:13:59.151
When you feel down,
pick up a 500-won coin on the street.

00:14:01.654 --> 00:14:03.030
Like a small win.

00:14:03.656 --> 00:14:06.408
That's what can change your mood.

00:14:07.368 --> 00:14:08.744
Willpower can't make that happen.

00:14:09.286 --> 00:14:11.413
That's why I take off running
from here every day.

00:14:12.539 --> 00:14:16.752
Here's to the joy of setting a new record!

00:14:53.914 --> 00:14:55.124
YOUR CURRENT SPEED
24 KM/H

00:14:55.708 --> 00:14:56.667
A new record!

00:15:12.891 --> 00:15:13.976
Have a good night.

00:15:14.059 --> 00:15:15.060
-Good night.
-Bye.

00:15:33.495 --> 00:15:35.372
HWANG DONG-MAN AND HIS BROTHER
NOT ALLOWED

00:15:35.456 --> 00:15:36.623
Writing a noir? Why?

00:15:36.707 --> 00:15:38.459
-Why not?
-Don't do it.

00:15:40.252 --> 00:15:41.086
There you are.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:43.338
You traitors.

00:15:44.256 --> 00:15:47.468
You having fun drinking at a place
your friend's banned from?

00:15:48.719 --> 00:15:49.887
Lee Jun-hwan!

00:15:50.387 --> 00:15:52.222
You might as well come out.

00:15:52.306 --> 00:15:53.932
Your shadow is a dead giveaway!

00:15:59.813 --> 00:16:01.065
Hey!

00:16:02.649 --> 00:16:05.152
-Jeez! Hey, pull him over.
-Is he insane?

00:16:05.861 --> 00:16:07.738
Jeez, you're such a handful.

00:16:09.031 --> 00:16:10.032
What the heck?

00:16:10.657 --> 00:16:12.367
-What are you doing?
-So then…

00:16:28.425 --> 00:16:29.343
Salute, sir.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.556
Did you know that Hitler resides in him?

00:16:35.849 --> 00:16:37.392
He has a desire

00:16:37.476 --> 00:16:41.522
to get rid of anyone
he finds incompetent or disapproves of.

00:16:42.397 --> 00:16:44.316
A strong urge to clear them out.

00:16:45.984 --> 00:16:46.860
Salute, sir!

00:16:56.286 --> 00:16:58.831
…and deliberately made time for us.

00:16:58.914 --> 00:16:59.915
Excuse me.

00:17:00.415 --> 00:17:01.250
Hye-jin.

00:17:02.626 --> 00:17:03.460
Just a moment.

00:17:04.753 --> 00:17:05.587
Tell me.

00:17:06.255 --> 00:17:08.048
Is there anyone you actually approve of?

00:17:08.132 --> 00:17:09.925
Everyone on the subway sucks, don't they?

00:17:10.926 --> 00:17:12.219
And they're all ugly.

00:17:13.178 --> 00:17:15.013
Might as well get rid of them
and live alone then.

00:17:18.016 --> 00:17:18.976
Does this mean

00:17:19.726 --> 00:17:21.353
I can also get rid of something

00:17:22.146 --> 00:17:24.940
that I don't approve of?

00:17:29.153 --> 00:17:31.363
I've been patient enough, you bastard!

00:17:33.824 --> 00:17:35.117
Hey, get back here!

00:17:36.869 --> 00:17:37.703
Hey!

00:17:40.914 --> 00:17:41.832
You little bastard.

00:17:42.374 --> 00:17:44.543
Damn it. You punk!

00:17:44.626 --> 00:17:47.462
You started this, so this is what you get!

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.798
What the hell is he saying?

00:17:50.382 --> 00:17:51.216
That little…

00:17:51.717 --> 00:17:52.926
Hwang Dong-man!

00:17:59.349 --> 00:18:01.977
This is the first time
anyone has come to my place.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.187
Wait, Jun-hwan's been here.

00:18:03.729 --> 00:18:05.522
Well, you're the first woman to visit.

00:18:05.606 --> 00:18:07.816
I think canned ham tastes better
than pork.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:11.570
If I had to choose between ham and pork
to take to a deserted island,

00:18:12.404 --> 00:18:13.322
I'd choose ham.

00:18:16.867 --> 00:18:17.701
Two eggs?

00:18:18.285 --> 00:18:19.119
Four?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.248
-Four eggs.
-Okay.

00:18:26.543 --> 00:18:27.628
One.

00:18:28.962 --> 00:18:29.963
Two.

00:18:34.927 --> 00:18:35.928
Four, right?

00:18:39.806 --> 00:18:40.724
The perfect trio.

00:18:47.105 --> 00:18:47.940
The perfect trio.

00:18:56.949 --> 00:18:57.783
What?

00:18:59.701 --> 00:19:00.661
Watch yourself.

00:19:02.162 --> 00:19:04.248
Or else I'll really lock you up
in a mental hospital.

00:19:07.084 --> 00:19:08.168
And the maintenance fee?

00:19:08.919 --> 00:19:10.003
I paid it.

00:19:12.089 --> 00:19:13.966
Don't drink on an empty stomach.

00:19:18.595 --> 00:19:20.764
SISTER VENGEANCE
STAGE GREETING

00:19:22.057 --> 00:19:24.893
The entire cast pushed themselves
to the breaking point.

00:19:24.977 --> 00:19:26.520
I hope you all enjoy the film,

00:19:26.603 --> 00:19:31.275
and please spread the word
about Sister Vengeance.

00:19:31.358 --> 00:19:32.609
Thank you!

00:19:35.988 --> 00:19:37.781
Hello, this is Jang Mi-ran.

00:19:37.864 --> 00:19:39.366
WE'RE HERE TO SEE YOU, MI-RAN!

00:19:39.992 --> 00:19:41.702
My body didn't actually break,

00:19:41.785 --> 00:19:43.120
but my arm did get wrecked.

00:19:44.454 --> 00:19:47.541
I worked so hard I couldn't tell
if I was sawing with my arm

00:19:47.624 --> 00:19:50.252
or sawing my arm off.

00:19:50.335 --> 00:19:52.254
Did you see
the weekend screening schedule?

00:19:52.879 --> 00:19:56.091
We need more afternoon showings
on the weekends.

00:19:56.174 --> 00:19:58.135
No one will watch it
if it's just mornings and nights.

00:19:58.677 --> 00:20:01.305
That's up to the distribution team.
You know the theaters don't listen to me.

00:20:01.847 --> 00:20:03.682
They only add showings for movies
that are selling.

00:20:05.225 --> 00:20:06.143
Then how about

00:20:06.977 --> 00:20:08.353
we hand out free tickets?

00:20:09.396 --> 00:20:11.315
Just 3,000.

00:20:12.024 --> 00:20:13.942
All right, I'll get to it.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:15.944
Okay.

00:20:18.405 --> 00:20:20.365
I'm the one who took the loss,

00:20:21.408 --> 00:20:22.909
so why are they the ones bitching?

00:20:51.271 --> 00:20:54.691
Director Park, I think your debut film
was your best work.

00:21:09.373 --> 00:21:11.166
-It's time to go now.
-Let's go.

00:21:16.797 --> 00:21:17.923
Man, these reviews…

00:21:23.762 --> 00:21:25.055
-Hey, it's Jang Mi-ran!
-Wow!

00:21:36.233 --> 00:21:37.984
I'm Director Park Gyeong-se.

00:21:41.738 --> 00:21:43.323
I just liked filmmaking…

00:21:45.075 --> 00:21:46.660
not knowing how tough it was.

00:21:53.083 --> 00:21:54.835
We worked really hard on this film.

00:22:15.522 --> 00:22:17.524
"I got mad and looked up
the director's films."

00:22:17.607 --> 00:22:20.569
"I haven't watched a single one.
I'll know to skip his work from now on."

00:22:22.654 --> 00:22:25.157
"A movie that spends the whole time

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:27.576
pretending to be cool and meaningful."

00:22:31.371 --> 00:22:32.747
"This is the first movie

00:22:33.582 --> 00:22:35.208
I've ever walked out of."

00:22:38.336 --> 00:22:39.296
"Hey, Director."

00:22:40.338 --> 00:22:41.548
"If you have a conscience,

00:22:42.924 --> 00:22:44.009
refund my 15,000 won

00:22:45.135 --> 00:22:46.595
for the ticket."

00:22:48.221 --> 00:22:49.347
"Refund my 15,000 won."

00:22:51.099 --> 00:22:52.100
My movie…

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:55.270
makes people want a refund.

00:22:55.353 --> 00:22:56.605
You can skip the movie…

00:22:57.230 --> 00:22:58.940
You can skip the movie…

00:22:59.024 --> 00:23:00.066
You can skip the movie…

00:23:01.151 --> 00:23:03.445
You can skip the movie and read about it
in group chats.

00:23:06.406 --> 00:23:07.532
"A movie so dull

00:23:08.408 --> 00:23:11.161
that you don't even get mad
when people text or take calls."

00:23:13.246 --> 00:23:14.539
"…when people text or take calls."

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.250
"I feel like murdering my friend

00:23:18.001 --> 00:23:19.461
who recommended this movie."

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:21.129
My movie

00:23:21.963 --> 00:23:23.506
drives people to murder.

00:23:24.883 --> 00:23:25.842
My movie

00:23:26.635 --> 00:23:29.387
drives people to murder.

00:23:36.144 --> 00:23:37.312
Gyeong-se isn't answering.

00:23:38.063 --> 00:23:39.356
Leave him alone.

00:23:40.398 --> 00:23:43.443
I never liked it when people
tried to make me feel better

00:23:44.486 --> 00:23:45.362
by texting or calling.

00:23:47.864 --> 00:23:49.282
You should've told me before I sent it.

00:23:50.825 --> 00:23:51.660
Darn it.

00:23:52.285 --> 00:23:53.286
THE EIGHT CLUB

00:23:54.371 --> 00:23:55.372
Huh?

00:23:56.289 --> 00:23:57.207
Did you know

00:23:57.832 --> 00:23:59.292
Gyeong-se was in the group chat?

00:23:59.793 --> 00:24:01.878
Yeong-su probably added him back in.

00:24:01.962 --> 00:24:04.714
When did he do that?

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:09.803
Damn it!

00:24:10.428 --> 00:24:11.513
Wait, this is…

00:24:12.389 --> 00:24:15.558
Gyeong-se keeps leaving every time
he's added back in,

00:24:15.642 --> 00:24:18.853
so Dong-man probably sent these messages,
thinking he'd left again.

00:24:18.937 --> 00:24:21.064
HOW DID THIS MOVIE
EVEN MAKE IT OUT INTO THE WORLD?

00:24:21.147 --> 00:24:23.108
I GUESS IT COMES DOWN TO
WHETHER YOUR WIFE IS AN EXECUTIVE PRODUCER

00:24:23.692 --> 00:24:25.318
Hwang Dong-man, that bastard.

00:24:25.402 --> 00:24:27.362
Why would he say this in our group chat?

00:24:27.445 --> 00:24:30.323
So no one noticed all the messages
he's been sending?

00:24:30.407 --> 00:24:31.658
Who bothers to read them?

00:24:31.741 --> 00:24:33.910
They're always about what he ate

00:24:33.994 --> 00:24:35.787
or what he watched or whatever.

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:37.205
He sends dozens of messages.

00:24:37.289 --> 00:24:39.791
I just go in to clear the unread count.

00:24:40.500 --> 00:24:42.794
-You don't read them either!
-Oh jeez.

00:24:43.753 --> 00:24:44.671
What's Gyeong-se doing?

00:24:46.589 --> 00:24:47.924
He went hiking in Jirisan.

00:24:50.927 --> 00:24:52.679
In any case,

00:24:53.430 --> 00:24:55.890
Gyeong-se can never see this.

00:24:56.516 --> 00:24:58.226
The unread count is still at one,

00:24:58.852 --> 00:24:59.728
so he hasn't read them.

00:24:59.811 --> 00:25:01.563
Just leave him alone for now.

00:25:01.646 --> 00:25:05.066
Don't call and tell him to leave the chat
without reading the messages.

00:25:05.150 --> 00:25:07.193
That'll just make him go in and read them.

00:25:07.986 --> 00:25:08.903
Just leave him alone.

00:25:08.987 --> 00:25:10.447
Leave him alone

00:25:10.530 --> 00:25:12.574
and pray that he'll leave the group chat.

00:25:13.158 --> 00:25:16.119
Hwang Dong-man, that little punk.

00:25:50.445 --> 00:25:51.279
What?

00:25:56.326 --> 00:25:57.160
Yeong-su.

00:25:58.161 --> 00:25:59.537
The number disappeared.

00:26:00.580 --> 00:26:01.414
What?

00:26:16.429 --> 00:26:19.808
Hwang Dong-man, you fucking bastard!

00:26:20.809 --> 00:26:22.977
You fucking bastard!

00:26:27.857 --> 00:26:29.651
-Here, Mr. Hwang.
-What?

00:26:34.364 --> 00:26:35.365
Thank you.

00:26:35.990 --> 00:26:38.076
Yeah, this one tastes the best.

00:26:38.618 --> 00:26:40.620
It's the bestseller at our store.

00:26:42.622 --> 00:26:44.582
-Tell your mother I said thank you.
-I will.

00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:50.088
I got up early today and did some writing
for the first time in a while.

00:26:50.171 --> 00:26:51.256
I was totally focused.

00:26:52.215 --> 00:26:54.175
I feel guilty for trying hard these days

00:26:54.259 --> 00:26:56.678
because I swore to live a worthless life.

00:26:57.846 --> 00:26:59.889
I can't help it because I'm having fun.

00:27:02.475 --> 00:27:04.144
But don't forget to live a worthless life.

00:27:04.227 --> 00:27:05.562
Right, live a worthless life.

00:27:07.772 --> 00:27:09.232
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:27:09.315 --> 00:27:10.942
Hey, eat before you go in!

00:27:11.985 --> 00:27:14.696
No change in advance ticket sales
despite giving out free tickets?

00:27:15.363 --> 00:27:16.239
None at all.

00:27:18.783 --> 00:27:20.368
Forget the marketing, then.

00:27:21.286 --> 00:27:22.829
Stop wasting money

00:27:22.912 --> 00:27:24.080
and just let it go.

00:27:27.041 --> 00:27:30.253
Who called the opening week numbers
for Sister Vengeance?

00:27:33.423 --> 00:27:37.177
The current number is about 310,000.

00:27:37.260 --> 00:27:38.303
No one came close, right?

00:27:40.263 --> 00:27:41.723
Someone called 300,000.

00:27:45.518 --> 00:27:46.352
Who?

00:27:47.645 --> 00:27:48.730
Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

00:28:03.036 --> 00:28:05.914
Lucky you for guessing correctly.

00:28:15.757 --> 00:28:17.467
What about the numbers for that one?

00:28:24.766 --> 00:28:26.351
Don't hold back. Just tell me.

00:28:31.189 --> 00:28:34.067
Can't you give it to me straight for once?

00:28:34.901 --> 00:28:36.486
How frustrating.

00:28:44.452 --> 00:28:46.746
I'm meeting Actor Song at Agit tonight.

00:28:46.830 --> 00:28:47.831
Come with me.

00:28:47.914 --> 00:28:49.457
Agit is like heaven these days

00:28:49.541 --> 00:28:51.459
now that Hwang Dong-man,
that pile of crap, isn't there.

00:28:51.543 --> 00:28:53.378
It feels like we've cleared out
ten years' worth of trash.

00:28:53.878 --> 00:28:55.797
He should've been banned a long time ago.

00:28:55.880 --> 00:28:58.633
But he keeps coming back,
only to be kicked out again.

00:28:58.716 --> 00:29:00.051
He's insane.

00:29:03.888 --> 00:29:04.848
Did you just sigh?

00:29:09.727 --> 00:29:10.812
No.

00:29:17.277 --> 00:29:19.070
Yes, you did. Why?

00:29:22.323 --> 00:29:23.324
Why did you sigh?

00:29:27.412 --> 00:29:29.122
What you said was too harsh.

00:29:30.915 --> 00:29:32.667
"Ten years' worth of trash."

00:29:34.711 --> 00:29:36.379
"A walking corpse."

00:29:36.963 --> 00:29:39.507
If I remember correctly,
you used to talk pretty harshly too.

00:29:40.133 --> 00:29:41.885
But you've lost your edge these days.

00:29:43.511 --> 00:29:45.513
You keep siding with Hwang Dong-man,

00:29:46.347 --> 00:29:48.474
but don't call us the bad guys

00:29:48.558 --> 00:29:49.642
without seeing what he's like.

00:29:53.313 --> 00:29:54.397
I'll see for myself.

00:30:06.951 --> 00:30:08.745
Did you see her talk back to me?

00:30:09.996 --> 00:30:14.459
I promoted her from office assistant
because she had an eye for screenplays.

00:30:14.542 --> 00:30:17.629
Now she's full of herself
and still hasn't come to her senses,

00:30:17.712 --> 00:30:19.172
even after screwing up.

00:30:20.882 --> 00:30:24.552
Director Park Su-hyeon still rages
when her name comes up,

00:30:24.636 --> 00:30:26.387
saying she's a crazy you-know-what.

00:30:26.471 --> 00:30:27.847
You're pulling another all-nighter?

00:30:28.723 --> 00:30:30.058
Where are you getting stuck?

00:30:30.141 --> 00:30:31.517
Tell me, and I'll sort it out.

00:30:33.603 --> 00:30:35.647
Or come out for a quick drink.

00:30:36.731 --> 00:30:38.942
Sitting there won't solve anything.

00:30:39.025 --> 00:30:40.568
Come eat before you get back to it.

00:30:41.235 --> 00:30:42.153
Okay, bye.

00:30:45.239 --> 00:30:46.324
Hey, why are you here?

00:30:47.450 --> 00:30:48.451
You know how it is.

00:30:48.534 --> 00:30:49.953
It's technically a group chat,

00:30:50.036 --> 00:30:52.080
but Dong-man made it his own private chat.

00:30:52.997 --> 00:30:54.707
No one knew
he was saying things like that.

00:30:55.208 --> 00:30:57.543
Jun-hwan has been so busy writing

00:30:58.336 --> 00:31:00.254
that he didn't really read them either.

00:31:00.338 --> 00:31:01.172
Right.

00:31:01.756 --> 00:31:04.509
I'm sure Dong-man didn't know
you were in the group chat.

00:31:05.802 --> 00:31:07.512
Slow down.

00:31:13.142 --> 00:31:14.060
Man, I'm starving.

00:31:14.143 --> 00:31:15.019
Excuse me!

00:31:15.895 --> 00:31:18.606
Can I get a bowl of rice
and a rolled omelet?

00:31:20.858 --> 00:31:22.902
Make it a cheese rolled omelet, please!

00:31:22.986 --> 00:31:23.945
Sure thing.

00:31:25.488 --> 00:31:28.741
If I'd known this was a kimchi stew place,
I wouldn't have come.

00:31:30.785 --> 00:31:32.078
Should I give it a shot?

00:31:32.704 --> 00:31:33.538
Should I try it?

00:31:37.417 --> 00:31:38.376
Hey, come on.

00:31:41.212 --> 00:31:42.547
Jeez, man.

00:31:56.644 --> 00:31:58.021
Looks like you went hiking.

00:31:58.855 --> 00:32:00.481
It's best when you need to
clear your head.

00:32:03.276 --> 00:32:04.402
Hang in there.

00:32:04.485 --> 00:32:06.112
-You crazy punk.
-What?

00:32:06.195 --> 00:32:07.030
Here, drink this.

00:32:14.704 --> 00:32:15.538
Goodness gracious.

00:32:16.998 --> 00:32:17.832
You know,

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:20.251
I can't even dream of hiking.

00:32:21.377 --> 00:32:24.088
I went to Seoraksan on a FAM tour
a long time ago,

00:32:24.172 --> 00:32:27.759
but I had to take a dump so bad
that I almost lost it running downhill.

00:32:27.842 --> 00:32:30.636
So now I break out in a cold sweat
whenever hiking comes up.

00:32:30.720 --> 00:32:32.680
I get anxious just looking at mountains.

00:32:33.473 --> 00:32:34.682
After that experience,

00:32:35.433 --> 00:32:37.894
I have nothing but respect for men
who go hiking.

00:32:38.895 --> 00:32:40.480
Which mountain did you go to?

00:32:46.903 --> 00:32:48.696
Why are you looking at me so lovingly?

00:32:50.073 --> 00:32:50.948
Tell me.

00:32:54.035 --> 00:32:55.453
You're enjoying this, aren't you?

00:32:57.080 --> 00:32:57.914
Yeah.

00:32:58.915 --> 00:32:59.749
Yeah.

00:33:00.374 --> 00:33:01.501
How did you know?

00:33:02.293 --> 00:33:03.628
I run around these days

00:33:04.253 --> 00:33:05.088
because I'm delighted.

00:33:08.758 --> 00:33:11.094
Put your hat back on.
You're hard to look at.

00:33:18.184 --> 00:33:20.603
I printed out the most scathing reviews

00:33:21.437 --> 00:33:23.481
and slowly read them out loud.

00:33:25.775 --> 00:33:27.276
I told myself to swallow them.

00:33:28.277 --> 00:33:30.071
If I couldn't swallow them,

00:33:30.822 --> 00:33:34.492
it felt like these bad reviews
would haunt me forever.

00:33:34.575 --> 00:33:36.619
So as I hiked up the mountain…

00:33:38.663 --> 00:33:41.249
I read each word carefully
and choked it down.

00:33:43.584 --> 00:33:45.419
Sweat streamed down my body,

00:33:46.379 --> 00:33:50.508
and I wasn't sure how I climbed up
as I kept mumbling the reviews.

00:33:50.591 --> 00:33:53.719
When I finally reached the summit
eight hours later,

00:33:54.595 --> 00:33:57.223
I thought I'd swallowed everything.

00:34:01.519 --> 00:34:03.437
Then I went into the group chat.

00:34:07.066 --> 00:34:07.900
That's right.

00:34:09.068 --> 00:34:10.653
I'm still in it.

00:34:13.865 --> 00:34:15.158
When I checked it,

00:34:16.450 --> 00:34:18.995
I saw the same words I had choked down.

00:34:20.913 --> 00:34:23.291
I guess you were impressed
with your own writing

00:34:23.374 --> 00:34:26.335
because it was posted
all over the internet.

00:34:26.419 --> 00:34:28.171
The words that went,

00:34:28.754 --> 00:34:30.214
"This is how good I am with words."

00:34:30.715 --> 00:34:33.509
"I guess whether
you become a director or not

00:34:35.303 --> 00:34:38.306
comes down to whether your wife
is an executive producer."

00:34:39.390 --> 00:34:42.018
"His wife spends a fortune
on her husband's hobby…"

00:34:46.230 --> 00:34:47.690
The one thing I was relieved about…

00:34:51.110 --> 00:34:53.654
was that Hye-jin
had already left the group chat.

00:34:56.157 --> 00:34:57.575
I noticed in the group chat…

00:34:59.952 --> 00:35:02.496
that one-third of the reviews
I had to choke down

00:35:03.998 --> 00:35:05.416
were written by you.

00:35:12.215 --> 00:35:17.345
I went to Jirisan at dawn
to force myself to choke down these words!

00:35:19.096 --> 00:35:21.307
Then I got so pissed
I ended up getting lost!

00:35:25.811 --> 00:35:28.231
I fought tooth and nail
to find my way back.

00:35:32.276 --> 00:35:35.905
I couldn't stand the idea of dying
without going straight for your throat,

00:35:37.365 --> 00:35:41.244
so I found a way down the mountain
like my life depended on it.

00:35:42.328 --> 00:35:43.371
-Hey.
-Gyeong-se.

00:35:49.710 --> 00:35:53.130
You asked how I had the nerve
to attend post-screening Q&amp;As.

00:35:54.173 --> 00:35:55.758
I feel like dying.

00:35:56.342 --> 00:35:57.969
Even the actors refuse to talk to me.

00:35:58.678 --> 00:36:00.388
I look at my phone in the waiting room.

00:36:01.013 --> 00:36:01.973
I feel like crying…

00:36:03.766 --> 00:36:05.268
being an outcast at my age.

00:36:08.521 --> 00:36:10.690
It's fine to go after me personally,

00:36:10.773 --> 00:36:15.361
but to attack my work like this
makes me feel like shit.

00:36:17.405 --> 00:36:19.073
I went through hell,
and I'm getting trashed.

00:36:19.156 --> 00:36:20.700
And the criticism is brutal.

00:36:22.535 --> 00:36:26.872
It feels like I've been stripped naked
and publicly dragged and shamed.

00:36:26.956 --> 00:36:28.582
I now feel compassion and respect

00:36:29.333 --> 00:36:31.961
for all the directors who came before me.

00:36:33.462 --> 00:36:35.756
They must've been
ripped to shreds like this…

00:36:37.633 --> 00:36:38.968
and been in so much pain.

00:36:42.555 --> 00:36:43.597
Hwang Dong-man,

00:36:44.849 --> 00:36:47.351
you've never been in the ring before.

00:36:47.935 --> 00:36:51.605
That's why you don't have any compassion
and just love it when people fail.

00:36:51.689 --> 00:36:53.024
That's the difference between us.

00:36:53.107 --> 00:36:54.608
It's a huge difference!

00:36:55.651 --> 00:36:57.069
It's the difference

00:36:58.112 --> 00:37:00.448
between a boxer
who's been beaten to a pulp in the ring

00:37:01.032 --> 00:37:03.909
and someone who's never stepped in one.

00:37:04.577 --> 00:37:08.247
It's like comparing someone already born
to someone not even born yet.

00:37:09.915 --> 00:37:10.833
Do you get it?

00:37:13.419 --> 00:37:14.253
You?

00:37:17.048 --> 00:37:18.674
You're just a nobody.

00:37:21.177 --> 00:37:22.053
Nothing.

00:37:22.136 --> 00:37:23.387
Nothing.

00:37:23.471 --> 00:37:24.805
Nothing!

00:37:28.642 --> 00:37:30.478
Park Gyeong-se, that bastard.

00:37:31.228 --> 00:37:35.691
How dare he? He calls that a movie?

00:37:36.233 --> 00:37:37.902
He hasn't made any good movies.

00:37:37.985 --> 00:37:39.320
That stupid bastard.

00:39:07.783 --> 00:39:08.784
Jin-man.

00:39:20.004 --> 00:39:21.172
What are you doing?

00:39:22.298 --> 00:39:23.674
Weren't you drinking?

00:39:27.011 --> 00:39:27.845
Jin-man.

00:39:31.307 --> 00:39:32.224
Come down.

00:39:40.733 --> 00:39:42.026
It's okay. Come down.

00:39:47.615 --> 00:39:48.908
You need to eat something.

00:39:50.701 --> 00:39:52.578
I'll make kimchi fried rice, so come down.

00:39:58.375 --> 00:39:59.835
Please come down, Jin-man.

00:40:59.979 --> 00:41:01.480
Hey, Jin-man.

00:41:02.189 --> 00:41:03.274
Want me to read you a poem?

00:41:04.400 --> 00:41:05.818
It's my favorite one.

00:41:07.653 --> 00:41:08.904
You wrote it

00:41:09.697 --> 00:41:13.033
when I was in middle school,
and I loved it so much

00:41:13.117 --> 00:41:15.536
that I hugged and kissed you
until you beat me up.

00:41:21.542 --> 00:41:22.376
The title is

00:41:23.586 --> 00:41:26.422
I Was a 0.2 mm Speck.

00:41:26.505 --> 00:41:27.840
EUNJEONG HIGH SCHOOL
LITERARY MAGAZINE

00:41:27.923 --> 00:41:29.633
A sperm is 0.001 mm

00:41:30.843 --> 00:41:32.428
An egg is 0.2 mm

00:41:34.138 --> 00:41:36.807
I mark the paper with a 0.2 mm dot

00:41:38.392 --> 00:41:39.476
That was me

00:41:41.103 --> 00:41:43.272
I was a 0.2 mm speck

00:41:46.358 --> 00:41:48.652
How did all this hatred fit in there?

00:41:50.362 --> 00:41:52.698
How did all this emptiness fit in there?

00:41:54.366 --> 00:41:55.701
My stomach churns

00:41:59.788 --> 00:42:02.374
A 0.2 mm fire ant passes by

00:42:03.751 --> 00:42:05.794
I crush it with my fingernail

00:42:09.423 --> 00:42:11.592
My hatred and emptiness

00:42:12.343 --> 00:42:14.011
Get crushed along with it

00:42:55.260 --> 00:42:56.178
Ms. Ko.

00:42:57.763 --> 00:42:58.681
Welcome.

00:42:59.598 --> 00:43:00.432
You're here.

00:43:00.516 --> 00:43:01.975
Congratulations!

00:43:02.059 --> 00:43:03.102
Congratulations.

00:43:04.895 --> 00:43:05.854
Thank you.

00:43:05.938 --> 00:43:07.147
It's good to see you.

00:43:07.940 --> 00:43:08.857
I'm excited to be here.

00:43:08.941 --> 00:43:11.485
KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK
BY MA JAE-YEONG

00:43:14.321 --> 00:43:15.447
I enjoyed it.

00:43:16.907 --> 00:43:20.452
Every character stands out,
and the story never loses momentum.

00:43:22.204 --> 00:43:23.122
Thank you.

00:43:23.205 --> 00:43:25.582
This is one of the top three screenplays
I've ever read.

00:43:28.627 --> 00:43:29.670
Thank you.

00:43:31.255 --> 00:43:33.549
And thanks for choosing Kopark Film
to handle the production.

00:43:34.133 --> 00:43:35.384
Of course, I'd choose Kopark Film.

00:43:39.680 --> 00:43:40.597
But you know what?

00:43:42.891 --> 00:43:45.561
I sense someone else
was involved in the screenplay.

00:43:49.940 --> 00:43:50.899
Oh.

00:43:53.193 --> 00:43:55.404
I just got some help

00:43:55.487 --> 00:43:56.405
from a friend.

00:43:59.324 --> 00:44:00.451
People like us can tell

00:44:01.452 --> 00:44:04.538
whether someone just gave advice
or actually had a hand in it.

00:44:07.207 --> 00:44:10.043
The way the characters talk
didn't come from you.

00:44:10.127 --> 00:44:11.170
It came from someone else.

00:44:12.588 --> 00:44:13.422
It was a woman.

00:44:16.049 --> 00:44:17.050
I know because I'm a woman.

00:44:17.968 --> 00:44:19.803
I can tell when a woman's lines

00:44:19.887 --> 00:44:21.680
were written by a man versus a woman.

00:44:21.764 --> 00:44:23.056
The same goes for you.

00:44:23.140 --> 00:44:25.893
You know when a man's lines
were written by a woman versus a man.

00:44:27.895 --> 00:44:31.064
There's an obvious female influence
in the screenplay.

00:44:31.690 --> 00:44:34.318
Is there a reason
she can't be the co-writer?

00:44:35.444 --> 00:44:37.988
Oh, she wasn't that involved.

00:44:38.071 --> 00:44:39.490
A co-writer?

00:44:40.199 --> 00:44:43.285
She just looked over it a bit,
but not enough to be credited.

00:44:45.078 --> 00:44:46.830
Does she know your screenplay
won the grant?

00:44:53.504 --> 00:44:55.964
This needs to be cleared up
from the start.

00:44:56.548 --> 00:44:58.509
It'll get messy
if this becomes an issue later.

00:45:05.516 --> 00:45:06.892
Goodbye.

00:45:14.650 --> 00:45:16.235
Are you less busy now?

00:45:19.279 --> 00:45:20.113
Yes.

00:45:20.781 --> 00:45:22.115
But I'm about to get busy again.

00:45:22.199 --> 00:45:23.825
I'm glad. It's good to be busy.

00:45:27.579 --> 00:45:30.165
WEATHER MAKER
BY HWANG DONG-MAN

00:45:36.588 --> 00:45:39.758
You still need to eat on time
even if you're busy.

00:45:40.592 --> 00:45:43.637
PRODUCER BYEON EUN-A

00:46:00.404 --> 00:46:01.655
I'm home.

00:46:01.738 --> 00:46:02.990
Are you just getting in?

00:46:06.535 --> 00:46:07.661
You're late.

00:46:28.765 --> 00:46:30.267
Why haven't you been replying to my texts?

00:46:38.650 --> 00:46:39.901
"I got the grant."

00:46:40.611 --> 00:46:41.820
"Thanks for your help."

00:46:44.197 --> 00:46:46.783
Want me to fill in the parts you left out?

00:46:48.910 --> 00:46:51.079
"Don't tell anyone
you were involved in my screenplay,

00:46:51.163 --> 00:46:52.998
or that you know me."

00:46:53.999 --> 00:46:56.627
"Don't even act like you know me."

00:47:01.423 --> 00:47:02.674
I'd appreciate that.

00:47:04.843 --> 00:47:06.595
It won't do either of us any good

00:47:06.678 --> 00:47:07.804
if word gets out we dated.

00:47:08.388 --> 00:47:10.390
That's not what you're afraid of.

00:47:11.725 --> 00:47:13.769
You're afraid of people finding out
we wrote it together.

00:47:14.811 --> 00:47:16.980
For fuck's sake.

00:47:21.068 --> 00:47:22.235
Hey.

00:47:22.819 --> 00:47:24.279
I've lost five teeth working on this.

00:47:25.072 --> 00:47:27.074
How dare you say we wrote it together?

00:47:41.713 --> 00:47:42.714
It really hurts

00:47:44.216 --> 00:47:46.468
to wish the worst on someone
I used to like.

00:47:49.221 --> 00:47:51.932
It feels like acid
being poured on my heart.

00:47:55.727 --> 00:47:57.104
But I won't take it anymore.

00:48:00.107 --> 00:48:02.150
Your cursing and violence

00:48:03.318 --> 00:48:05.737
made up only 3% of our time together.

00:48:07.280 --> 00:48:09.366
But now you're trying to undermine

00:48:09.449 --> 00:48:11.743
the other 97% of the time
when we were okay.

00:48:12.703 --> 00:48:14.246
So I'll have to respond in kind.

00:48:18.375 --> 00:48:20.961
Now all that's left
is that 3% of bitter fighting.

00:48:28.218 --> 00:48:29.678
Put my name on the screenplay,

00:48:30.303 --> 00:48:32.055
or take out all the parts I wrote.

00:48:32.931 --> 00:48:36.059
We exchanged emails,
so you'll know which parts I wrote.

00:48:40.814 --> 00:48:42.232
I wish you'd just die.

00:48:57.080 --> 00:48:58.832
There are tons of people like you
in this industry.

00:48:59.499 --> 00:49:01.543
People who can't write anything
on their own,

00:49:01.626 --> 00:49:03.211
yet tell others how to write

00:49:03.295 --> 00:49:05.005
and try to go along for the ride.

00:49:08.300 --> 00:49:09.384
Is it Hwang Dong-man this time?

00:49:11.636 --> 00:49:13.346
I hear you only review leftovers

00:49:13.972 --> 00:49:15.640
since you can never get a good one.

00:49:17.934 --> 00:49:19.186
Seriously.

00:49:20.729 --> 00:49:21.688
Aren't you embarrassed

00:49:22.606 --> 00:49:23.982
to be involved with a loser like him?

00:49:38.079 --> 00:49:38.997
Damn it!

00:49:55.180 --> 00:49:57.140
A man on the verge of success

00:49:57.224 --> 00:49:58.809
is easily blinded.

00:50:01.144 --> 00:50:02.604
And they can easily become a bad guy.

00:50:08.443 --> 00:50:11.863
Everyone here has been through the same.

00:50:17.619 --> 00:50:20.330
And everyone is still ashamed
about what they did.

00:50:21.790 --> 00:50:24.042
I love that they know how to feel ashamed.

00:50:27.671 --> 00:50:29.256
People who remain blinded

00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:31.758
and driven by ruthless ambition

00:50:31.842 --> 00:50:34.427
and selfish desires are not allowed here.

00:50:36.263 --> 00:50:37.472
So what about you?

00:50:39.516 --> 00:50:41.434
Will you get yourself banned,

00:50:41.518 --> 00:50:44.104
or will you be someone
who lives with shame for a long time?

00:50:53.196 --> 00:50:56.533
If you wanted all the credit,
you should've pursued a solo art form,

00:50:57.576 --> 00:50:59.536
not filmmaking,
where 200 people collaborate.

00:52:04.392 --> 00:52:06.728
I can't believe you said
you were delighted.

00:52:09.189 --> 00:52:10.273
I felt my stomach drop.

00:52:12.150 --> 00:52:13.735
We have to keep seeing each other,

00:52:13.818 --> 00:52:15.528
so you have to watch what you say.

00:52:16.738 --> 00:52:18.198
You know he's having a rough time.

00:52:19.908 --> 00:52:23.912
I'm not asking for much, am I?

00:52:23.995 --> 00:52:26.748
Can't you just be kind to him?

00:52:28.166 --> 00:52:29.250
Is that so hard to do?

00:52:30.210 --> 00:52:32.420
Kindness is basic human decency, right?

00:52:34.047 --> 00:52:35.548
Jeez.

00:52:36.216 --> 00:52:37.092
Yeong-su.

00:52:38.343 --> 00:52:39.594
I'm really sad.

00:52:40.470 --> 00:52:43.348
How could you ask me
to be kind to those guys?

00:52:43.932 --> 00:52:45.850
I'm really good at telling

00:52:47.268 --> 00:52:50.188
who likes me and who doesn't.

00:52:51.356 --> 00:52:52.983
When I'm with someone who likes me,

00:52:53.608 --> 00:52:54.901
I become really gentle.

00:52:55.902 --> 00:52:57.028
My body responds.

00:52:57.612 --> 00:52:59.906
My blood pressure and heart rate drop.

00:53:00.991 --> 00:53:03.910
It's an instinctive reaction
that all animals share.

00:53:04.494 --> 00:53:05.662
I feel really grateful

00:53:06.830 --> 00:53:09.416
when someone chooses to sit next to me
in a coffee shop.

00:53:09.499 --> 00:53:11.710
I even put my hands together and pray

00:53:13.586 --> 00:53:15.672
that they have a wonderful day.

00:53:18.049 --> 00:53:21.720
I'm just mad I don't have enough luck
to make that wish last more than a day.

00:53:21.803 --> 00:53:22.971
That's who I am.

00:53:23.555 --> 00:53:25.181
If you show me an ounce of kindness,

00:53:25.265 --> 00:53:27.017
I'll do anything for you.

00:53:28.268 --> 00:53:30.645
So why do I have to be kind to people
who hate me?

00:53:35.900 --> 00:53:38.653
I'm not the one you should be talking to.
Talk to those guys!

00:53:41.322 --> 00:53:42.157
You know,

00:53:43.491 --> 00:53:45.076
I'm like a litmus test strip.

00:53:45.577 --> 00:53:47.996
If the other person is acidic,
I'm acidic too.

00:53:48.079 --> 00:53:50.248
If they're alkaline, I'm alkaline as well.

00:53:50.832 --> 00:53:52.709
You're not aware of this…

00:53:54.961 --> 00:53:56.921
but I'm a freaking lovable guy.

00:54:03.887 --> 00:54:06.389
They say catching falling leaves
brings good luck.

00:54:07.766 --> 00:54:09.684
I'm passing along the luck I caught.

00:54:18.902 --> 00:54:22.280
Do you know what my emotion watch says
whenever I see my friends?

00:54:23.907 --> 00:54:24.991
Not me.

00:54:27.035 --> 00:54:29.204
-He's your senior, right?
-I'm clean.

00:54:30.955 --> 00:54:31.790
What's that?

00:54:34.167 --> 00:54:37.128
Oh, it's clean because of that?

00:54:37.212 --> 00:54:38.546
Come on, that's enough.

00:54:40.507 --> 00:54:41.341
"Anxious."

00:54:43.635 --> 00:54:44.677
I had no idea

00:54:45.303 --> 00:54:46.638
I felt that anxious.

00:54:48.473 --> 00:54:49.891
If I wedge myself into a place

00:54:50.475 --> 00:54:52.185
where I'm not welcome,

00:54:52.644 --> 00:54:53.937
how could I not feel anxious?

00:54:55.230 --> 00:54:57.649
So I talk my head off
to overcome that anxiety.

00:54:58.900 --> 00:55:01.820
I laugh and talk until tears come out,

00:55:02.695 --> 00:55:06.282
but when my emotion watch vibrates,
and I look down at it,

00:55:07.450 --> 00:55:08.952
do you know what it says?

00:55:11.496 --> 00:55:12.497
"Fed up."

00:55:12.580 --> 00:55:14.874
FED UP

00:55:44.154 --> 00:55:45.697
How long am I banned for?

00:55:46.281 --> 00:55:47.574
Until you get a girlfriend.

00:55:50.618 --> 00:55:53.830
That'll knock some sense into you
much faster than wearing that watch.

00:55:54.664 --> 00:55:57.167
Talk to a woman. Hug her. Sleep with her.

00:55:57.250 --> 00:55:58.293
Then you'll come to your senses.

00:56:00.128 --> 00:56:04.716
You're not brave enough
to grow old and die on your own.

00:56:06.634 --> 00:56:07.594
So find a woman.

00:56:18.146 --> 00:56:19.647
People who like me

00:56:20.440 --> 00:56:21.941
ease my anxiety,

00:56:22.901 --> 00:56:26.654
so I don't have to act out like crazy.

00:56:54.891 --> 00:56:56.017
Eun-a.

00:56:58.561 --> 00:57:02.065
RESTRICTED AREA
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

00:57:21.000 --> 00:57:22.043
Grandma.

00:57:24.629 --> 00:57:26.256
Do you have a 500-won coin?

00:57:35.223 --> 00:57:36.933
When I get nosebleeds…

00:57:41.604 --> 00:57:44.232
my whole body hurts
like it's being torn apart.

00:57:46.025 --> 00:57:47.986
I'm in excruciating pain one moment…

00:57:50.280 --> 00:57:52.365
Don't act like you're the adult here.

00:57:52.448 --> 00:57:54.075
Nobody here asked you to.

00:57:54.158 --> 00:57:56.869
And just you wait.
I'm about to become something incredible.

00:57:56.953 --> 00:57:59.038
Look forward to my shiny story.

00:58:00.498 --> 00:58:01.541
Then suddenly,

00:58:03.126 --> 00:58:04.294
just like that,

00:58:06.045 --> 00:58:07.213
the pain disappears.

00:58:08.339 --> 00:58:09.757
As if a knot

00:58:10.592 --> 00:58:13.303
just slips loose.

00:58:14.220 --> 00:58:16.598
What does your watch say then?

00:58:20.727 --> 00:58:21.811
"Relieved."

00:58:21.894 --> 00:58:23.771
RELIEVED

00:59:12.320 --> 00:59:14.322
Whenever I come across
a similar situation,

00:59:15.990 --> 00:59:19.911
I'm right back at that moment,
paralyzed with fear.

00:59:21.204 --> 00:59:22.872
Back to when I was helpless.

00:59:24.791 --> 00:59:27.085
Back in the classroom
where I couldn't leave.

00:59:28.670 --> 00:59:30.004
Back when I was nine.

00:59:32.590 --> 00:59:35.009
Back when I couldn't even breathe

00:59:36.469 --> 00:59:38.221
in front of the people who crossed me off…

00:59:40.139 --> 00:59:42.308
and all I could do
was to helplessly wait for death.

00:59:44.352 --> 00:59:45.478
Who do you think it was?

00:59:47.355 --> 00:59:48.398
Who do you think

00:59:49.065 --> 00:59:50.692
was the first person to cross you off?

01:00:01.035 --> 01:00:01.869
M…

01:00:03.538 --> 01:00:04.455
O…

01:00:06.207 --> 01:00:07.083
T…

01:00:09.210 --> 01:00:10.044
H…

01:00:13.423 --> 01:00:14.799
E…

01:00:14.882 --> 01:00:17.260
MOTHE…

01:00:29.147 --> 01:00:30.565
That word…

01:00:36.195 --> 01:00:37.780
is so overrated.

01:02:06.828 --> 01:02:07.787
Jeez, you scared me.

01:02:31.102 --> 01:02:31.978
Can you guess…

01:02:34.146 --> 01:02:35.481
what just popped up?

01:02:38.860 --> 01:02:39.694
"Shocked."

01:02:40.987 --> 01:02:41.863
"Flustered."

01:02:42.905 --> 01:02:43.781
"Worried."

01:02:45.741 --> 01:02:46.784
It didn't say "excited."

01:02:49.871 --> 01:02:50.705
Gosh, I…

01:02:51.664 --> 01:02:53.583
I was really surprised.

01:02:58.838 --> 01:03:02.133
I'm not a destructive person!

01:03:03.092 --> 01:03:06.137
I'm not a monster!

01:03:33.331 --> 01:03:34.498
Where do you live?

01:03:40.755 --> 01:03:42.798
I'll scatter 500-won coins for you!

01:03:42.882 --> 01:03:44.216
Where do you live?

01:04:12.286 --> 01:04:14.163
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:04:32.264 --> 01:04:33.683
Did you see the social media post?

01:04:33.766 --> 01:04:35.977
Her husband raised their kid.
She wasn't neglected.

01:04:36.060 --> 01:04:39.814
One wrong move and Oh Jeong-hui
can kiss her career goodbye.

01:04:40.356 --> 01:04:42.650
-No way.
-Read this, Hwang Dong-man.

01:04:42.733 --> 01:04:44.652
I bet Hwang Dong-man
wants to die right now.

01:04:44.735 --> 01:04:45.861
Damn it!

01:04:45.945 --> 01:04:47.279
Hwang Dong-man, did you read it?

01:04:49.198 --> 01:04:50.533
Where are you going?

01:04:50.616 --> 01:04:52.535
Tell me a funny story.

01:04:52.618 --> 01:04:54.954
Don't fight the thing
that's giving you a hard time, Eun-a.

01:04:55.037 --> 01:04:56.288
It's like sleep paralysis.

01:04:56.372 --> 01:04:57.957
I always chose to avoid them.

01:04:58.040 --> 01:05:01.043
But this time,
I'm going to put them in their place.

01:05:01.127 --> 01:05:02.545
We should meet. Come outside.

01:05:02.628 --> 01:05:06.173
So? Did you choke down every last word?

01:05:08.926 --> 01:05:13.931
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim